      "text": "PhotoCraft is an open-source, cross-platform raster graphics editor developed by ArtCraft as a drop-in replacement for Adobe Photoshop. Built in Rust with a native compositor targeting Metal, Vulkan, DirectX 12, and WebGPU, it replicates Photoshop's UI, shortcuts, layer system, adjustment layers, filters, smart objects, and PSD/PSB file format with byte-for-byte round-trip accuracy. It runs offline, requires no web runtime, and is positioned as the first release in ArtCraft's broader strategy to recreate proprietary creative software as community-owned, AI-extensible alternatives."
