    "summary": "ArtCraft, a fledgling company founded by Brandon Thomas, presented its ambitious open-source strategy at the AI Engineer Code Summit in San Francisco. The centerpiece is PhotoCraft, a Photoshop-compatible image editor written entirely in Rust that runs natively on Metal, Vulkan, DirectX 12, and WebGPU without Electron. The application achieves near-perfect PSD/PSB round-trip fidelity — 134 of 135 real-world test files match byte-for-byte — and replicates Photoshop's menus, shortcuts, panels, and tools including 16 adjustment layers, 70-plus live-preview filters, and smart objects. ArtCraft has released 17 open-source clones of popular software tools to date, and Thomas signaled intentions to extend the approach beyond imaging, having already replicated Adobe Acrobat. The project's public parity tracker on GitHub documents ongoing compatibility work against Photoshop 26.6.1.",
